## Offline Review

Regenerate the release-candidate evidence report without connecting to Unreal Editor:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\review_mcpweather_release_candidate_evidence.py check
```

Expected result:

- `status=pass`
- `release_status=pass`
- `failed_check_count=0`

## Finalize Dry Run

Run the finalizer without deleting anything:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\finalize_mcpweather_release_candidate_after_editor_close.py run
```

Expected result:

- `status=pass`
- `mode=dry_run`
- `delete_cleanup=false`
- `cleanup.pending_or_deleted_package_count=4` while the current temp packages still exist.

## Cleanup After Editor Close

Only after Unreal Editor is closed and the dirty map state has been intentionally resolved, run:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\finalize_mcpweather_release_candidate_after_editor_close.py run --delete-cleanup
```

This command must refuse to delete while `UnrealEditor.exe` is active. When it succeeds, it runs a post-delete dry-run verification expecting zero selected temp packages.

Equivalent explicit cleanup commands are:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\promote_niagara_mcpweather_source_template.py cleanup --name-prefix NS_MCPWeatherPromotion_20260630_promotion_release_gate_contract_no_execute_ --delete
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\promote_niagara_mcpweather_source_template.py cleanup --name-prefix NS_MCPWeatherPromotion_20260630_release_candidate_execute_v1_ --delete
```

Do not run those explicit `--delete` commands while Unreal Editor is open.

## Strict Gate After Editor Restart

When the editor has been restarted cleanly, prefer the split gate for one more release-candidate confidence pass:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_mcpweather_niagara_split_release_gate.py live --run-id 20260630_release_candidate_split_strict_after_restart_v1 --rain-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_ReleaseCandidate_20260630_Rain --snow-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_ReleaseCandidate_20260630_Snow --run-visual-regression --run-plugin-independence --preset-retries 1
```

The split gate is preferred after long editor sessions because it records per-preset attempts and avoids losing already-passed evidence when one preset preview times out.

The combined gate remains valid after a clean restart:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\release_gate_mcpweather_niagara.py live --run-id 20260630_release_candidate_full_strict_after_restart_v1 --rain-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_ReleaseCandidate_20260630_Rain --snow-system-path /Game/MCPWeather/Generated/NS_MCPWeather_ReleaseCandidate_20260630_Snow --run-visual-regression --run-plugin-independence
```

## Release Contracts

- The final assets must not depend on UnrealMCP. Keep the static scan markers at `/Script/UnrealMCP`, `/UnrealMCP`, `UnrealMCP`, `MCPUnreal`, and `mcp_unreal`, and keep the isolated `-DisablePlugins=UnrealMCP -EnablePlugins=PythonScriptPlugin` load check.
- Snow must keep `/Game/MCPWeather/FX/Snow/Materials/M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle.M_MCPWeather_Snow_Particle` on every enabled Sprite renderer through `primary_material` or `used_materials`.
- Rain release preview should keep the conservative defaults: 6 frames, 480 promoted post-setup settle frames, and 300 second command timeout.
- Generated temp cleanup must stay clamped to `/Game/_MCP_Temp/NiagaraGenerated`.
- Promotion and finalization should keep dry-run behavior as the default unless intentionally writing or deleting content.

## Final Handoff State

The release candidates are currently acceptable from the recorded evidence. The remaining operational work is maintenance cleanup after editor close, followed by an optional strict split gate after editor restart if another live visual confidence pass is desired.
